summary":"Is used to denote Proconsular Asia, a Roman province which embraced the western parts of Asia Minor, and of which Ephesus was the capital, in Acts 2:9; 6:9; 16:6; 19:10, 22; 20:4, 16, 18, etc., and probably Asia Minor in Acts 19:26, 27; 21:27; 24:18; 27:2.","verses":18,"v":[4]},{"id":"patmos_926","name":"Patmos","kind":"Island","lat":37.30752,"lon":26.54827,"summary":"A small rocky and barren island, one of the group called the “Sporades,” in the AEgean Sea. It is mentioned in Scripture only in Rev. 1:9. It was on this island, to which John was banished by the emperor Domitian (A.D. 95), that he received from God the wondrous revelation recorded in his book.","verses":1,"v":[9]},{"id":"ephesus_400","name":"Ephesus","kind":"City","lat":37.94194,"lon":27.33972,"summary":"The capital of proconsular Asia, which was the western part of Asia Minor. It was colonized principally from Athens. In the time of the Romans it bore the title of “the first and greatest metropolis of Asia.”","verses":17,"v":[11]},{"id":"laodicea_716","name":"Laodicea","kind":"City","lat":37.83692,"lon":29.10786,"summary":"The city of this name mentioned in Scripture lay on the confines of Phrygia and Lydia, about 40 miles east of Ephesus (Rev. 3:14), on the banks of the Lycus.","verses":6,"v":[11]},{"id":"pergamum_937","name":"Pergamum","kind":"City","lat":39.11895,"lon":27.16513,"summary":"The chief city of Mysia, in Asia Minor. One of the “seven churches” was planted here (Rev. 1:11; 2:17). It was noted for its wickedness, insomuch that our Lord says “Satan’s seat” was there.","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"philadelphia_941","name":"Philadelphia","kind":"City","lat":38.34905,"lon":28.51946,"summary":"Brotherly love, a city of Lydia in Asia Minor, about 25 miles south-east of Sardis. It was the seat of one of the “seven churches” (Rev. 3:7-12).","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"sardis_1027","name":"Sardis","kind":"City","lat":38.47683,"lon":28.11413,"summary":"The metropolis of Lydia in Asia Minor. It stood on the river Pactolus, at the foot of mount Tmolus. Here was one of the seven Asiatic churches (Rev. 3:1-6).","verses":3,"v":[11]},{"id":"smyrna_1103","name":"Smyrna","kind":"City","lat":38.45196,"lon":27.16192,"summary":"Myrrh, an ancient city of Ionia, on the western coast of Asia Minor, about 40 miles to the north of Ephesus. It is now the chief city of Anatolia, having a mixed population of about 200,000, of whom about one-third are professed Christians.","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"thyatira_1160","name":"Thyatira","kind":"City","lat":38.92293,"lon":27.84052,"summary":"A city of Asia Minor, on the borders of Lydia and Mysia. Its modern name is Ak-hissar, i.e., “white castle.” Here was one of the seven churches (Rev. 1:11; 2:18-28).","verses":4,"v":[11]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["sabbath-and-lords-day",10,10],["reading-revelation",1,3],["reading-revelation",19,19]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[602,602,602,602,2424,2424,5547,3739,2316,1325,846,1166,1166,846,1401,3739,1163,5034,1096,1096,1096,4591,4591,4591,4591,1223,649,846,32,3588,846,1401,2491],[3739,3140,3140,3745,3708,3708,3588,3588,3588,3056,2316,2316,2532,3588,3141,2424,2424,5547],[3107,3107,3588,3588,3588,314,314,3588,3056,3588,3588,4394,2532,2532,2532,3588,3588,191,2532,5083,3588,1125,1125,1722,846,1063,3588,2540,2540,1451],[2491,3588,3588,2033,1577,1722,773,773,773,773,5485,2532,1515,4771,4771,575,3588,3588,1510,2532,1510,2532,2064,2064,2064,2532,575,3588,2033,4151,1799,846,2362],[2532,575,2424,5547,3588,4103,3144,3588,4416,3588,3588,3498,2532,3588,758,3588,3588,935,3588,3588,1093,3588,3588,3588,25,1473,2532,3089,3089,1473,1537,1473,266,1722,846,129],[2532,4160,4160,1473,1473,1473,932,932,2409,3588,846,2316,2532,3962,846,846,3588,1391,2532,2904,165,3588,165,281],[2400,2064,2064,2064,3326,3588,3507,2532,3956,3788,3708,3708,846,3748,3748,1574,846,2532,3956,3588,5443,3588,3588,1093,2875,2875,1909,1909,846,3483,3483,3483,3483,281],[1473,1510,3588,1,2532,3588,5598,3